# Tactile Slip Reflex — CNL Spec
# Demo 2: A 3-neuron SNN implements a biological slip reflex.
# FSR detects slip → interneuron gates response → motor neuron tightens grip.
# Target latency: comparable to biological reflex arc (~50ms).

The network MUST operate WITH timestep of 1 ms

The network MUST contain an excitatory sensory population of 1 neurons
The network MUST contain an excitatory interneuron population of 30 neurons
The network MUST contain an excitatory motor population of 1 neurons

# Sensory population fires when FSR detects slip (force drop)
The sensory population MUST fire ONLY IF membrane potential exceeds 0.5

# Interneuron gates reflex response
The interneuron population MUST fire ONLY IF membrane potential exceeds 0.6

# Motor population fires to tighten grip
The motor population MUST emit a spike ONLY IF membrane potential exceeds 0.7

# Tight refractory periods for fast reflex response
The sensory population MUST NOT fire DURING the refractory period of 0.001 seconds
The motor population MUST NOT fire DURING the refractory period of 0.002 seconds

# Fast membrane dynamics for reflex-speed response
The sensory population membrane potential MUST decay WITH time constant of 0.005 seconds
The motor population membrane potential MUST decay WITH time constant of 0.01 seconds

# Strong sensory-to-motor coupling for reliable reflex
The sensory population MUST project to interneuron population
The interneuron population MUST project to motor population
The sensory population MUST project to motor population

The connection from sensory population to interneuron population MUST have WITH synaptic weight of 1.6
The connection from interneuron population to motor population MUST have WITH synaptic weight of 2.0
The connection from sensory population to motor population MUST have WITH synaptic weight of 0.4

# Short axonal delay modelling biological interneuron latency
A synapse MUST have a transmission delay of 3ms
